&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Corporate Strategy &amp;amp; Development&lt;/strong&gt;, you will work in a small, AI enabled team of highly driven and committed individuals, reporting to the Director Corporate Strategy &amp;amp; Development. This is a high-exposure role, acting as the strategic and analytical engine for our most important decisions in a team that reports &lt;strong&gt;directly to the Group CEO&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the team&#39;s full agenda: Group and business unit strategy, portfolio and capital allocation decisions, and M&amp;amp;A. You are hands-on: you build the financial models, analysis and executive-level outputs yourself. You work under the guidance of the team leadership, owning the quality of analysis and models within your workstreams as well as the respective internal stakeholder relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the development of the Group&#39;s mid-term strategy by driving the process, own the underlying analysis, strategic synthesis, and preparation of strategic documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Unit Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as an internal consultant, supporting our key business units across geographies on a project-by-project basis to develop their mid-term strategies and solve their most complex challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;M&amp;amp;A Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive workstreams for M&amp;amp;A projects, building and owning financial models, analyzing targets, preparing negotiations and supporting the M&amp;amp;A processes the team owns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portfolio Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the strategic analysis for key portfolio decisions, including potential geo-expansions, new vertical or brand launches or divestments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capital Allocation:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and improve the analytical frameworks and models to support our strategic budget allocation and ROI analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;4+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of high-performance experience from a top-tier Management Consulting firm, Investment Banking, or a comparable in-house Strategy / Corporate Development team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Toolkit:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional qualitative and analytical problem-solving skills. You are hypothesis-driven and can own and structure complex analytical problems from end-to-end. You are utilizing AI tools to meaningfully improve your productivity. Ability to build applications with AI coding tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong financial modeling skills are required: you have built and defended models used for investment or strategic decisions. Valuation experience is a plus. You are just as comfortable building analysis and models from scratch as you are managing processes and presenting recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DTC economics:&lt;/strong&gt; You are comfortable working with typical DTC KPIs like CAC, AOR, AOV, CLV, retention and understand how cohort economics build a P&amp;amp;L over time. DTC marketing analytics experience is a plus but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactive 360° communication and excellent ability to synthesize complex analysis into clear, concise storylines, presentations&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;and memos for an executive audience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you work:&lt;/strong&gt; You take ownership of outcomes and pressure-test your own conclusions before presenting them. You go deep into the analysis to get to the right answer, and know when it is good enough to decide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
